# Copy to .env.local (git-ignored) only if you want local dev to use a real
# database. Without any of these, `npm run dev` uses an in-memory store.
# On Vercel, set them under Settings → Environment Variables (or let a
# Marketplace integration add them). Use ONE of the two options.

# Option 1: Upstash REST (added by the "Upstash for Redis" integration)
# KV_REST_API_URL=https://<your-db>.upstash.io
# KV_REST_API_TOKEN=<token>

# Option 2: any Redis connection string (Redis Cloud, the "Redis" integration, …)
# REDIS_URL=redis://default:<password>@<host>:<port>
